From: Security Engineering <security-engineering@company.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Remove obsolete gl_PREREQ_EXPLICIT_BZERO for RHEL 9 compatibility

The gnulib macro gl_PREREQ_EXPLICIT_BZERO is not recognized by RHEL 9's
packaged autotools, causing autoreconf to fail. This macro is obsolete
and not required for pam_tacplus v1.7.0.

Remove the single offending line from configure.ac.

---
 configure.ac | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -XX,7 +XX,6 @@
 AC_CONFIG_MACRO_DIR([m4])
 AC_CONFIG_HEADERS([config.h])
- gl_PREREQ_EXPLICIT_BZERO
 AM_INIT_AUTOMAKE([1.11 foreign no-dist-gzip dist-bzip2])
--
2.39.0
